# ─── Dependencies and build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
out/
build/
*.tgz

# ─── Logs, caches, test artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.eslintcache
.npm/
.cache/

# ─── Secrets and credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing matching these has ever been committed. The rules exist so that a
# stray copy dropped into the checkout cannot be staged by accident.
# Note: no *.gpg rule. installer/husk-apt.gpg is the PUBLIC apt signing key and
# is tracked on purpose; the private key lives only in the APT_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY
# repository secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.provisionprofile

# ─── Editor and OS files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ─── Local Husk data and config ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# These belong on the user's machine, not in source. Anchored to the repo root
# so a legitimate config.json or data/ elsewhere in the tree is still tracked.
/config.json
/data
.husk-tmp/
MEMORY/
**/voice-models/

# Screen recordings used to produce docs/images/*.gif. The optimised GIFs are
# committed; the source MP4 / MOV stays local.
docs/*.mp4
docs/*.mov

# ─── Bundled PAI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ship the framework only. Personal PAI data (memory, learning, credentials,
# user-specific extensions) must never enter the repo, even if a sync tool
# copies a populated ~/.claude tree into libs/pai.
libs/pai/PAI/USER/**
!libs/pai/PAI/USER/**/
!libs/pai/PAI/USER/**/README.md
libs/pai/**/MEMORY/
libs/pai/**/LEARNING/
libs/pai/**/.credentials.json
libs/pai/**/ratings.jsonl
libs/pai/**/*reflections*.jsonl
libs/pai/**/history.jsonl

# The same private-data shapes under ANY vendored framework, not just the one
# that happened to be vendored first. Re-vendoring under a new directory name
# otherwise arrives with no protection, and a missing ignore rule is silent
# until a sync tool drops real data in. Templates stay tracked: these match
# populated data, and every shipped USER file declares template provenance.
libs/**/MEMORY/
libs/**/LEARNING/
libs/**/.credentials.json
libs/**/ratings.jsonl
libs/**/*reflections*.jsonl
libs/**/history.jsonl

# ─── Agent tooling artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-session identity files Husk rewrites at runtime.
.github/copilot-instructions.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.husk-aider.md
.husk-autopilot-status.json

# aider's local artifacts (chat history, input history, tags cache).
.aider*

# Claude Code's local state. Nothing here is shipped; force-add if a shared
# agent config is ever committed deliberately.
.claude/

# PAI Algorithm task artifacts (per-task working state, never shipped).
ISA*.md

# Local exposure scanning suite. Deliberately not tracked: it exists to be run
# before a push to main, from a pre-push hook, so its findings and reports stay
# on this machine rather than in a public repository or a world readable CI log.
scripts/exposure/
docs/exposure-runbook.md
